   logical, and delimiter operators.
3. Syntax Analysis & AST: Handwritten recursive descent parser enforcing operator
   precedence climbing (||, &&, ==, !=, <, <=, >, >=, +, -, *, /, %, unary -, !).
   Constructs a clean AST representing programs, functions (e.g., int main()),
   variable declarations, array declarations, loops (for, while), conditions (if/else),
   and return statements.
4. Semantic Analysis: Symbol table with lexical scoping tracking symbol name, type,
   array properties, size, line, column, and scope level. Verifies undeclared variables,
   duplicate definitions, indexing non-arrays, array initializer count overflows,
   division by zero in constant literals, and static array bounds checks.
5. Compiler Orchestration: Pure Python module (Compiler) executing Lexer -> Parser ->
   Semantic Analyzer with clear stage status tracking (success, error, skipped).
